{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1273077-inspiration","id":1273077,"title":"Inspiration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-06T05:41:10-08:00","id":1273077,"title":"Inspiration","content":"I just could not get into American Gods when it premiered but, after playing the demo, I want to give it another shot. What other media do you use as inspiration for Scion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T06:50:40-08:00","id":1273088,"title":"","content":"Depends on the tone of the game I'm going for. I really love Rick Riordan's Percy Jackson, Kane Chronicles, and Magnus Chase series for modern myth stories. For something a little darker or more mature, I actually think that superhero comics show a lot of interesting concepts about how society would shape around people with power on an entirely different scale.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just remembered another one. Check out &quot;The Secrets of the Immortal Nicholas Flamel&quot;. Lots of gods, monsters, and magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":18560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","user":"saedar","date":". 12-06-2018, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T15:01:06-08:00","id":1273153,"title":"","content":"George O'Connor's The Olympians series of graphic novels. They're retellings of the old Greek stories, but done wonderfully and in a way that makes the various gods feel like real people. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T11:14:04-08:00","id":1273285,"title":"","content":"The Almighty Johnsons is pretty good inspiration, especially if you want some comedic inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T14:44:27-08:00","id":1273325,"title":"","content":"I really miss stuff from less popular mythologies, like Orish\u00e1s, Teotl, Sh\u00e9n, Devas, etc. The Kami have a lot of manga/anime representation. Most of pop culture focus more in Aesir/Theoi stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T01:39:21-08:00","id":1274005,"title":"","content":"Now while it's not a good inspiration for actual folklore, I like the animated series &quot;Hilda&quot; on Netflix as inspiration. Not for material, but for TONE.<br /> <br /> Hilda is a show where the mythic and magical is... Y'know just kind of accepted as a Thing in the world. When the main character, Hilda, tells her mom that she's friends with a small elf and watches trolls in the wild, her mom never doubts her. Hell, the city they move to, Trollberg, has a giant wall around it to keep out trolls, and the local hardware store sells troll repellent. Monsters, spirits, and magic exist... And nobody doubts this. It's exactly the kind of feeling I want to evoke in my Scion games, where the mythic is <i>very much </i>a known thing and part of life in the World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T11:15:23-08:00","id":1274085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hayashi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1273077-inspiration?p=1273325#post1273325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really miss stuff from less popular mythologies, like Orish\u00e1s, Teotl, Sh\u00e9n, Devas, etc. The Kami have a lot of manga/anime representation. Most of pop culture focus more in Aesir/Theoi stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea as to how much is translated and the like, but I would think that there has to be a bunch of stuff for the Deva too, given the thriving entertainment industry in India.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T15:58:07-08:00","id":1274113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1273077-inspiration?p=1274085#post1274085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No idea as to how much is translated and the like, but I would think that there has to be a bunch of stuff for the Deva too, given the thriving entertainment industry in India.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's also Nollywood in Nigeria, but I have no idea how much their movies touch on traditional legends and the likes of the Orisha or Alusi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T08:22:07-08:00","id":1274204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1273077-inspiration?p=1274085#post1274085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No idea as to how much is translated and the like, but I would think that there has to be a bunch of stuff for the Deva too, given the thriving entertainment industry in India.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only are there a number of movies and TV shows in several languages about the Deva, the Indian Film Industry has even given us a full on Goddess... Santoshi, Goddess of Satisfaction and Daughter of Ganesha, essentially had her Legend wholesale created in a 60's Bollywood Movie and currently has temples and festivals in her name <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T14:40:01-08:00","id":1274250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1273077-inspiration?p=1274113#post1274113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There's also Nollywood in Nigeria, but I have no idea how much their movies touch on traditional legends and the likes of the Orisha or Alusi.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Searching at the moment for Oya - Rise of the Orisha. Watched a teaser, got positively impressed. Reccomend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T18:20:07-08:00","id":1274291,"title":"","content":"Just read The Great God Pan by Arthur Machen and Helen Vaughn is a particularly terrifying example of just how disturbing a Scion of a wilderness/fertility/sex god can be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T23:57:10-08:00","id":1274509,"title":"","content":"The webcomic Godslave follows Edith, a twenty-something who accidently breaks a canopic jar in a museum and frees something that looks like a fennec fox/dog hybrid with red fur and a forked tail. It tells her that he is Anpu, the Egyptian god of the dead, and that his family imprisoned him because they wanted to stop the cycle of Ma'at while they were in power. He imbues her with one of his ba so that she can survive against the blacksmith agent of Heru who was also at the museum.<br /> <br /> Edith knows nothing about Egyptian mythology, so the audience is introduced to it along with her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.godslavecomic.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.godslavecomic.com/comics/1793324400-07-142.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.godslavecomic.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> Godslave </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.godslavecomic.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.godslavecomic.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Edith has been thrown into the danger of Egyptian mythology in the modern day. Fighting monsters and family drama of godly proportions. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T14:27:38-08:00","id":1274624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>karpomatic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1273077-inspiration#post1273077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just could not get into American Gods when it premiered but, after playing the demo, I want to give it another shot. What other media do you use as inspiration for Scion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Try the book if you haven\u2019t read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T14:57:48-08:00","id":1274782,"title":"","content":"Probably already know of the Wicked and the Divine, but it's of course natural. Especially with Kieron Gillen writing that intro. Also, this retelling of the Taking of Persephone is kinda pseudo-modern and might get you in the right place. <a href=\"https://www.webtoons.com/en/romance/lore-olympus/list?title_no=1320&amp;page=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.webtoons.com/en/romance/...no=1320&amp;page=1</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T07:01:41-08:00","id":1275494,"title":"","content":"Just remembered a good example of Mantles in media. Comes from Dresden Files and how Odin is presented.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Odin is depicted as all of, 1.) typical one-eyed sage/trickster powerful god, 2.) Santa Clause, 3.) the King of the Unseelie faeries. All seem to have different responsibilities and personality quirks.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":18560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","user":"saedar","date":". 12-23-2018, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T07:20:28-08:00","id":1275502,"title":"","content":"I've been listening to The Magnus Archive podcast and later seasons have things (the fears) which could map to gods with some of the human characters being Scions or Demi-Gods. CoD might be a better fit for the feel of the podcast, but if you wanted to make it a bit more action-oriented, I think Scion would work well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T13:41:06-08:00","id":1276307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saedar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1273077-inspiration?p=1275494#post1275494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue anima